.\" Manpage for pluto.
.\" Process with: groff -man -Tutf8 pluto.1
.TH PLUTO 1 "2026-04-15" "pluto 0.3" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
pluto \- Haiku-native Claude client (CLI and GUI)

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pluto
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-one-shot\fR \fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B pluto agent
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B pluto routine
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B pluto schedule
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B pluto trust
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B pluto mcp
\fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.br
.B pluto login | logout | stats
.br
.B Pluto-gui

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pluto
is a native Haiku client for the Anthropic Claude API, written in C++17
against libcurl and the Be API. It provides an interactive REPL, a
one-shot mode for scripting, a Model Context Protocol (MCP) client with
HTTP/SSE/stdio transports, eight built-in tools (read_file, write_file,
edit_file, bash, grep, glob, desktop_script, clipboard), six native
Haiku tools that operate on BFS extended attributes and BQuery
(read_attr, write_attr, list_attrs, remove_attr, query_fs, live_query),
and a node_monitor tool for watching filesystem changes.
.PP
.B pluto
also includes an agent store, routine engine, schedule manager,
workspace trust system, skill/command extensibility, OAuth 2.0
authentication, and local telemetry.
.PP
.B Pluto-gui
is a separate binary built from the same core, providing a native
.B BWindow
interface with split chat/detail view, collapsible tool blocks,
markdown rendering, syntax highlighting, inline diff viewer, image
previews, streaming cursor, context-window gauge, BFS-backed session
storage, Deskbar replicant, and notifications on turn completion.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " NAME"
Provider name: \fBanthropic\fR (default) or \fBopenai-compat\fR
(Ollama, OpenRouter, LM Studio, or any OpenAI-compatible server).
.TP
.BI \-\-model " ID"
Model identifier (e.g. \fBclaude-opus-4-6\fR, \fBllama3.1\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-base\-url " URL"
Override the API base URL. Required for \fBopenai-compat\fR provider
(e.g. \fBhttp://localhost:11434\fR for Ollama).
.TP
.B \-\-yolo
Auto-approve every tool call. Use with care.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Disable ephemeral
.B cache_control
on system prompt and tool definitions.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the request that would be sent without calling the API.
.TP
.BI \-\-one\-shot " TEXT"
Send a single prompt, print the response, and exit. No REPL.
.TP
.BI \-p " TEXT" "\fR, \fB" \-\-prompt " TEXT"
Headless mode: send a single prompt with auto-approved tool calls,
print output to stdout, and exit. Suitable for scripting and CI.
.TP
.BI \-f " FMT" "\fR, \fB" \-\-format " FMT"
Output format for headless mode: \fBtext\fR (default, streaming) or
\fBjson\fR (structured object with text, tokens, tool_calls).
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress status messages on stderr (headless mode).

.SH REPL COMMANDS
Inside the interactive prompt:
.TP
.B /help
List commands.
.TP
.B /quit
Exit.
.TP
.B /reset
Clear conversation history.
.TP
.B /plan
Toggle plan mode (read-only analysis). Write tools are disabled and the
model is instructed to describe changes without making them.
.TP
.B /tools
List registered tools.
.TP
.BI /init " [--force]"
Create a
.I pluto.md
project memory file in the workspace root. Auto-detects language, build
system, and git remote. Use
.B \-\-force
to overwrite an existing file.
.TP
.BI /model " ID"
Switch model for subsequent turns.
.TP
.B /cost
Show session token totals.
.TP
.BI /save " [title]"
Save current session to BFS store.
.TP
.BI /load " <query|idx>"
Load a session by title substring or `/list` index.
.TP
.B /list
List saved sessions, sorted by most recent.
.TP
.B /resume
Load the most recently updated session.
.TP
.B /delete
Delete the current session file.
.TP
.BI /title " <new>"
Set the session title used on next /save.
.TP
.BI /tag " [name]"
Show tags or add one to the current session.
.TP
.BI /untag " <name>"
Remove a tag from the current session.
.TP
.BI /watch " [URL]"
Subscribe to an SSE stream and inject events into context. Default
.B http://localhost:2607/sse.
.TP
.B /unwatch
Stop the SSE subscription.
.TP
.B /events
Show pending SSE events without sending a new turn.
.TP
.B /routines
List available routines with schedule and status.
.TP
.BI /routine " NAME"
Expand a routine's template and send it as a prompt in the current chat.
.TP
.B /commands
List custom slash commands from
.IR ~/config/settings/pluto/commands/ .

.SH INPUT FEATURES
.TP
.BI @ file.txt
Include the contents of a file in the message. Multiple
.B @
mentions are expanded before sending.
.TP
.BI @ image.png
Attach an image (PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP, up to 20 MB) as a vision
content block. Supports base64 encoding for both Anthropic and
OpenAI-compatible providers.

.SH AGENT SUB-COMMAND
.TP
.B pluto agent list
List installed agents with version and description.
.TP
.BI "pluto agent install " "<path|url> [--trust]"
Install an agent from a local directory or Git URL. Shows the agent
prompt for review before installing; use \fB--trust\fR to skip review.
.TP
.BI "pluto agent remove " NAME
Remove an installed agent and unregister its skills, routines, and commands.
.TP
.BI "pluto agent update " "<name> | --all"
Update an agent from its original Git source. Compares versions and
reinstalls if a newer version is available. Use \fB--all\fR to check
all agents with a source URL.
.TP
.BI "pluto agent info " NAME
Show agent metadata and prompt body.
.TP
.BI "pluto agent search " QUERY
Search installed and example agents by name, description, author, or
tools (case-insensitive substring match).
.TP
.BI "pluto agent run " FILE.md
Run a prompt file as a one-shot agent with auto-approved tool calls.

.SH ROUTINE SUB-COMMAND
.TP
.B pluto routine list
List routines with status, schedule, and model.
.TP
.BI "pluto routine run " NAME
Execute a routine (expands templates, runs via agent mode).
.TP
.BI "pluto routine enable " NAME
Enable a routine (rewrites frontmatter).
.TP
.BI "pluto routine disable " NAME
Disable a routine.
.TP
.BI "pluto routine install " NAME
Install a launch_daemon job for a scheduled or file-watch routine.
.TP
.BI "pluto routine uninstall " NAME
Remove the launch_daemon job.
.TP
.BI "pluto routine log " NAME
Show the last 50 lines of the routine's execution log.

.SH SCHEDULE SUB-COMMAND
.TP
.B pluto schedule list
List configured schedules with status.
.TP
.BI "pluto schedule add " "NAME --file FILE [--event boot|login] [--interval MINS] [--model ID]"
Create a new schedule. Supports periodic (interval) and event-based
(boot/login via launch_daemon) triggers.
.TP
.BI "pluto schedule remove " NAME
Remove a schedule and its launch_daemon job.
.TP
.BI "pluto schedule enable " NAME
Enable a schedule.
.TP
.BI "pluto schedule disable " NAME
Disable a schedule.
.TP
.BI "pluto schedule run " NAME
Run a schedule immediately.

.SH TRUST SUB-COMMAND
.TP
.B pluto trust list
List permanently trusted workspace directories.
.TP
.BI "pluto trust add " PATH
Trust a directory permanently (persisted in trusted_workspaces).
.TP
.BI "pluto trust remove " PATH
Remove a directory from the trusted list.
.TP
.B pluto trust log
Show the last 50 lines of the access log (allow/deny decisions).

.SH AUTHENTICATION
.TP
.B pluto login
Start OAuth 2.0 + PKCE login flow for Claude Max/Pro plans. Opens a
browser for authentication and stores tokens in
.IR ~/config/settings/pluto/oauth-tokens .
.TP
.B pluto logout
Remove stored OAuth tokens. Falls back to API key if set.

.SH TELEMETRY
.TP
.B pluto stats
Show aggregated token usage, turn counts, session counts, and estimated
cost per model. Requires opt-in via
.BR "touch ~/config/settings/pluto/telemetry" .
.TP
.B pluto stats reset
Clear the telemetry CSV file.

.SH MCP SUB-COMMAND
.TP
.B pluto mcp list
List configured MCP servers across all scopes.
.TP
.BI "pluto mcp add " "NAME [--url URL | --command CMD] [--scope user|project|local]"
Add a server.
.TP
.BI "pluto mcp remove " NAME
Remove a server.
.TP
.BI "pluto mcp get " NAME
Show details for a server.

.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGINT (Ctrl+C)
While a turn is streaming, aborts the in-flight HTTP request via the
curl progress callback. The REPL keeps running; press Ctrl+C again at
an empty prompt to quit (or use
.BR /quit ).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/config
Main configuration file (key=value). Keys: provider, model, base_url,
api_key_env, system, max_tokens, context_window, cache, font_delta,
hook_pre_tool, hook_post_tool, hook_user_prompt.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto-api-key
Fallback for the API key when the environment variable is empty.
chmod 600.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/oauth-tokens
OAuth 2.0 access and refresh tokens (chmod 600). Written by
.BR "pluto login" .
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/sessions/
Directory containing JSONL session files. Each file has BFS
attributes (
.BR pluto:title ", " pluto:model ", " pluto:tags ", " pluto:tokens_in ", " pluto:tokens_out ", " pluto:created ", " pluto:updated ", " pluto:turns
) and is searchable from Tracker's Find dialog.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/pluto.md
User-wide memory file, appended to the system prompt as
.BR <user_memory> .
.TP
.I ./pluto.md
Project-scoped memory file, appended to the system prompt as
.BR <project_memory> .
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/skills/<name>/SKILL.md
Skill definitions. Always-on skills are injected into the system prompt.
Skills with a
.B trigger:
frontmatter line are loaded on demand when the user message matches.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/commands/<name>.md
Custom slash commands. Optional
.B description:
frontmatter. The body supports
.B {{args}}
substitution.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/routines/<name>.md
Routine definitions with YAML frontmatter (name, schedule, model,
tools, notify, enabled).
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/agents/<name>/
Installed agents. Each has an AGENT.md and optional skills/, routines/,
commands/ subdirectories. A .agent-source file stores the Git URL for
updates.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/schedules/<name>.conf
Schedule configuration files.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/trusted_workspaces
List of permanently trusted directories (one per line).
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/access.log
Audit log of workspace allow/deny decisions with timestamps.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/telemetry
Empty marker file; its existence enables local telemetry.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/stats.csv
Token usage CSV (model, tokens_in, tokens_out, turns, sessions).
.TP
.I ./.mcp.json
Project-scoped MCP server configuration. Each new server prompts for
approval on first use.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/mcp.json
User-scoped MCP server configuration.
.TP
.I ~/config/settings/pluto/mcp-local.json
Local (per-cwd) MCP server configuration.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
API key. Takes precedence over the on-disk fallback. The variable name
can be overridden with the
.B api_key_env
config key.
.TP
.B PLUTO_LOG
Set to \fBdebug\fR to enable verbose logging to stderr. Shows cache
stats, retry details, and MCP tool counts.

.SH BUGS
GUI tool approval blocks the worker thread on a semaphore released by
the UI thread. Closing the window while a tool approval alert is open
may stall briefly. Mitigation: dismiss the alert before quitting.

